2 CONT Nauvoo, Hancock, Illinois, USA, BURI Nauvoo) = SEYMOUR BRUNSON (1798-1840), early Mormon convert,
2 CONT missionary, High Councilor of the Commerce/Nauvoo Stake, lieutenant colonel in the Hancock County
2 CONT Militia, bodyguard of Joseph Smith; at his funeral (15 Aug 1840) Joseph Smith first publicly
2 CONT presented the doctrine of baptism for the dead; named in D&C 75:33 and D&C 124:132. Evidence: Church
2 CONT History Biographical Database (official - Born Plattsburg, Clinton, New York, 1 Dec 1798 EXACT;
2 CONT Father Reuben Brunson EXACT; Mother Sarah Clark EXACT; Died Nauvoo, Hancock, Illinois, 10 Aug 1840
2 CONT EXACT; D&C 75:33 + D&C 124:132) + Wikipedia (exact-subject article - parents 'Reuben and Salley
2 CONT Clark Brunson'; married Harriet Matilda Gould 1823, seven children; died Aug 10, 1840; funeral
2 CONT baptism-for-the-dead first presentation) + D&C Central / ScriptureCentral (died Aug 10, 1840 at
2 CONT Joseph Smith's home, Nauvoo; funeral Aug 15, 1840; D&C 124:132) + Latter Day Light (died Aug 10,
2 CONT 1840, age 41 years 8 months 9 days = BIRT 1 Dec 1798 EXACT by arithmetic; buried Nauvoo Pioneer
2 CONT Cemetery with military honors). New combined source @S900000098@ (N-13).
2 CONT ADJUDICATION (N-3): identity unambiguous - name + BIRT 1 Dec 1798 Plattsburgh NY + DEAT 10 Aug 1840
2 CONT Nauvoo + parents Reuben Brunson / Sarah Clark + wife Harriet Matilda Gould all match the official
2 CONT Church source EXACTLY. Tree data kept verbatim (N-5): Wikipedia's BIRT 18 Sept 1799 Virginia =
2 CONT VARIANCE vs Church DB + import (1 Dec 1798, Plattsburgh NY) - not adopted; the Church DB is official
2 CONT and corroborated by the 41y-8m-9d age-at-death arithmetic, which lands exactly on 1 Dec 1798.
2 CONT OPEN QUESTIONS (N-22 marker attached): (1) NO FAMS @F10112@ carried - tree WIFE @I232102454130@
