2 CONT SEYMOUR BRUNSON (verified; married about 1822-1824, Hector, New York), mother of his seven children
2 CONT including LEWIS BRUNSON (verified); after Seymour's 1840 death she married JOHN ELMER and traveled
2 CONT west to Utah with her sons Lewis and Seymour Jr., dying in Fillmore in 1879. Evidence: Wikipedia
2 CONT (exact-subject Seymour Brunson article - 'In 1823, Brunson married Harriet Matilda Gould. They
2 CONT eventually had seven children') + Latter Day Light ('In about 1822 Seymour Brunson and Harriet
2 CONT Matilda Gould were married. Harriet was born August 11, 1802, in Hector, Schuyler County, New
2 CONT York'; 'Only Lewis and Seymour, Jr. remained in the church and traveled West with Harriet') +
2 CONT FamilyCentral (Harriet Matilda GOULD b. 11 Aug 1802 Hector, Seneca, New York; d. 31 Jul 1879
2 CONT Fillmore, Millard, Utah EXACT vs tree; marriage 1824 Hector, Seneca, New York) + Book of Mormon
2 CONT Evidence (FamilySearch memory: 'Harriet married John Elmer' after Seymour's death). New combined
2 CONT source @S900000099@ (N-13).
2 CONT ADJUDICATION (N-3): identity unambiguous - the 'Harriet Matilda Gould' name + wife-of-Seymour +
2 CONT DEAT 31 Jul 1879 Fillmore UT match all sources. Tree data kept verbatim (N-5): BIRT 11 Aug 1801 =
2 CONT 1-year VARIANCE vs latterdaylight + familycentral (11 Aug 1802) - not adjudicated; Hector's county
2 CONT (Schuyler vs Seneca vs Tompkins across sources) is county-boundary changes (Hector was in Seneca,
2 CONT then Tompkins; Schuyler formed 1854), not a conflict; MARR year 1822/1823/1824 varies by source
2 CONT OPEN QUESTIONS (N-22 marker attached): (1) NO FAMC @F900008199@ carried - tree parents unverified as
