1 NOTE VERIFIED 02 OCT 2026 (historical fast-track, ledger 20261002-0238): @I232117316399@ = BODEGISEL (also Bodygisil), Frankish duke (dux), son of Mummolin duke of Soissons; served the kings Chilperic I and Childebert II; dux of Provence; celebrated in song by the contemporary poet Venantius Fortunatus; rector of Marseilles under Sigebert I until c. 565; accompanied Rigunth to Spain 584; murdered at Carthage on the return from a Constantinople embassy (585 or 588). Gregory of Tours records him passing his estate to his heirs undiminished. Evidence: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bodegisel (exact-subject, read 01 Oct 2026) + medieval.eu 'The Merovingian Sarcophagus of Chrodoara' (read 02 Oct 2026), which reports duke Bodegisel as 'known from the writings of Gregory of Tours and a poem of Venatius Fortunatus', citing Stiennon (1979) and Gauthier (1993).
2 CONT ADJUDICATION (N-3): the tree record is a CONFLATION - the historical dux Bodegisel overlaid with the semi-legendary 9th-c 'Boggis' of Aquitaine (per Herrmann & Nonn, confusion of Bodegisel with the later duke Bobo; Sigebert of Gembloux misplaces Boggis c. 711). Tree data kept verbatim (N-12): BIRT 0545/550 Tongeren; DEAT 588 Carthage matches scholarly 585/588 Carthage EXACTLY; DEAT 6 July 0607 Tongeren is the conflated Boggis layer (unattested); BURI Metz unconfirmed; 'Governor d'Aquitaine' / 'Meroving' name-glitter ASSERTED (unattested on either source).
2 CONT New combined source @S900000089@ (N-13). OPEN QUESTIONS (N-22 marker attached): (1) tree parentage @F900002449@ (St Gendolfus Bishop of Tongeren-Maastricht + Palatina 'Queen of Aquitaine') CONTRADICTS both sources' 'son of Mummolin, duke of Soissons' - the scholarly filiation is not carried as the tree's parents; (2) the Chrodoara-of-Amay marriage rests on the 13th-c Vita sanctae Odae ('according to this [13th-c vita] Chrodoara had married a Frankish duke called Bodegisel' - medieval.eu) - NOT admitted without better attestation.
1 NOTE BUILD: @I232117316399@ carried as an INDIVIDUAL only. Excluded per N-21, mapped: NO FAMC @F900002449@ (tree parents match NONE of the scholarly filiation - scholarly: son of MUMMOLIN duke of Soissons; parentage NOT carried, candidates remain unadjudicated); NO FAMS @F900002455@ (Bodegisel + Chrodoara of Amay) and NO FAMS @F900003974@ (Bodegisel + Oda of Suevia) - neither source attests either marriage (the Chrodoara link is 13th-c vita material embedded in the Boggis conflation); per the 2026-10-01 task instruction, a parent link for Arnulf of Metz (@I232109311779@, verified) is admitted ONLY if both sources attest it - Wikipedia EXPLICITLY negates the inference (Gregory 'does not explicitly identify Bodegisel's heirs - notably, it does not prove that he was the father of Arnulf of Metz'); medieval.eu attests only the person, no family links. Backlog section 0(a) 'person verification' item TICKED; the 'Arnulf parent link' item stays OPEN (documented, not admitted).
