1 NOTE VERIFIED 21 SEP 2026 (historical fast-track, ledger 20260921-2355): this is
2 CONT Frederick II of Diessen (also Frederick I of Regensburg; 1005-1075), German
2 CONT nobleman, documented as bailiff (Vogt/Domvogt) of the Regensburg cathedral chapter
2 CONT in 1035; count in the Sempt area from 1055; died 1075 as a lay brother in
2 CONT Sankt Blasien Abbey in the Black Forest - one of the earliest known ancestors
2 CONT of the Counts of Andechs (House of Andechs). Evidence:
2 CONT en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_II,_Count_of_Diessen + fmg.ac MedLands BAVARIAN
2 CONT NOBILITY (GRAFEN von DIESSEN: "FRIEDRICH [III], son of FRIEDRICH [II] Graf &
2 CONT his wife --- (-30 Jun 1075, bur Seeon)"; charter dated [1030] "comes Friderich
2 CONT et filius eius Friderich"; grants 13 Mar 1055 / 10 Dec 1055 "in comitatu
2 CONT Friderici comitis"; necrology of Seeon "II Kal Jul 1075 ... Fridricus com de
2 CONT Andex et hic iacet").
