2 CONT Frederick I (c.912 - 18 May 978), count of Bar and duke of Upper Lorraine,
2 CONT founder of the House of Bar / House of Ardennes-Bar (cadet branch of the House
2 CONT of Ardenne); son of Wigeric of Lotharingia (Wigeric de Bidgau, count of Bidgau,
2 CONT count palatine of Lorraine) and Cunigunda of France; sixth-generation descendant
2 CONT of Charlemagne; m. 954 Beatrice, daughter of Hugh the Great (count of Paris) and
2 CONT Hedwig of Saxony; installed 959 as duke of Upper Lotharingia (with Godfrey in
2 CONT Lower), styling himself duke after Bruno's death in 977; children Henry (d.
2 CONT 972-978), Adalbero II (958-1005, bishop of Verdun and Metz), Theodoric I
2 CONT (965-1026). Evidence: en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frederick_I,_Duke_of_Upper_Lorraine
2 CONT (read this run: c.912 - 18 May 978; son of Wigeric and Cunigunda; m. Beatrice
2 CONT 954; refs Le Jan 2003, Nash 2017, Wickham 2009, Evergates 1995, Reuter 1992,
2 CONT Leyser 1994) + fmg.ac MedLands CAPET.htm (read this run: 'm (Betrothed 951,
2 CONT [10 Sep/12 Nov] 954) FREDERIC Comte, son of WIGERICH [III] Graf im Bidgau,
2 CONT Pfalzgraf & his wife Cunegondis --- ([910/15]-[Jun/Jul] 978)'; installed in 959
2 CONT as FREDERIC I Duke of Upper Lotharingia; cites Flodoard 954 MGH SS III p.402,
2 CONT Gesta Episcoporum Virdunensium MGH SS X p.492, Alberic de Trois-Fontaines
2 CONT MGH SS XXIII p.767). The older-mirror 'c.942' birth (en-academic.com, 1066.co.nz
