1 TITL WIKIPEDIA: Robert I, Count of Flanders (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_I,_Count_of_Flanders, search text read 24 Sep 2026 - exact-subject article: 'Robert I (c. 1035 - 13 October 1093), known as Robert the Frisian, was count of Flanders from 1071 until his death in 1093. He was a son of Count Baldwin V'; Spouse Gertrude of Saxony; Issue 'Robert II, Count of Flanders, Adela, Gertrude'; infobox Father Baldwin V of Flanders, Mother '?'; refs Murray 1989, Tanner 1992) + WikiTree Flandre-14 (search text read 24 Sep 2026: 'Robert l, Count of Flanders (c. 1033-1093) was also known as Robert the Frisian ... His parents were Baldwin V of Flanders and Adele (Capet), a daughter of King Robert ll (Capet) of France'; 'In 1063 Robert l, Count of Flanders married Gertrude of Saxony, dowager countess of Holland ... they had 6 children: Robert II ... Adelais (died 1115) ... Gertrude, who became duchess of Lorraine ... Philipp ... Ogiva')
0 @S900000057@ SOUR
1 TITL WIKIPEDIA: Gertrude of Saxony (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gertrude_of_Saxony, search text read 24 Sep 2026 - exact-subject article: 'Gertrude of Saxony (c. 1030 - August 4, 1113), also known as Gertrude Billung, was a countess of West-Frisia by marriage to Floris I, Count of West-Frisia, and countess of Flanders by marriage to Robert I, Count of Flanders'; 'She was the daughter of Bernard II, Duke of Saxony and Eilika of Schweinfurt'; 'In 1063 Gertrude married Robert of Flanders (Robert the Frisian)'; Issue: Albert, Dirk V, Peter, Bertha of Holland, Floris, Matilda, Adela, Robert II Count of Flanders, Gertrude of Flanders Duchess of Lorraine, Philip of Loo, Ogiva; refs Wiszewski 2010) + fmg.ac MedLands SAXONY (search text read 24 Sep 2026): 'c) GERTRUD of Saxony (Schweinfurt [1028]-Veurne 4 Aug 1113, bur Veurne). The Genealogica Comitum Flandriae Bertiniana names "filiam Bernardi Saxonum comitis Gertrudem" as wife of "Robertus", specifying that she was "viduam Florentii comitis Fresonum" ... "Gertrudis" is named as wife of "Roberti Frisonis" in the Cartulaire de Saint-Bertin ... The Genealogia ex stirpe Sancti Arnulfi names "Idam Namucensem ... et Gertrudem comitissam Flandrensem" as children of "Bernardum"'
0 @S900000054@ SOUR
1 TITL WIKIPEDIA: Henry III, Count of Louvain (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_III,_Count_of_Louvain, search text read 24 Sep 2026 - 'Henry III of Louvain (German: Heinrich, Dutch: Hendrik, French: Henri; died 1095), was Count of Louvain (Leuven) and Landgrave of Brabant, son of Henry II (c. 1020-1078), Count of Louvain and Brussels, and Adela of Orthen (or Betuwe)'; 'In July 1095, he took part in a tournament in Tournai ... mortally wounded'; 'About 1090 he married Gertrude of Flanders (1080-1117), daughter of Robert I of Flanders and Gertrude of Saxony') + fmg.ac MedLands BRABANT, LOUVAIN ch.2 (v5.0, updated 27 Jun 2025, opened 24 Sep 2026): 'a) HENRI de Louvain (-killed in a tournament Tournai 5 Feb 1095, bur Nivelles) ... He succeeded his father in [1078/79] as HENRI [III] Comte de Louvain ... married "filie Roberti Flandriensis comitis" and died "in single combat" at Tournai ... m as her first husband, GERTRUDE de Flandre, daughter of ROBERT I Count of Flanders & his wife Gertrud of Saxony [Billung] (-[1115/26])'
0 @S900000055@ SOUR
1 TITL WIKIPEDIA: Adelaide of Leuven (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adelaide_of_Leuven, search text read 24 Sep 2026 - exact-subject article: 'Adelaide of Leuven (died c. 1158) was the wife of Simon I, Duke of Lorraine (1076-1138) ... She was the daughter of Henry III of Leuven and his wife Gertrude of Flanders'; retired to Tart Abbey after 1138; children Matthias I, Robert, Agatha, Hedwige, Bertha, Mathilde, Baldwin, John; refs Epistolae/Columbia) + fmg.ac MedLands BRABANT, LOUVAIN ch.2 (v5.0, opened 24 Sep 2026): 'Comte Henri [III] & his wife had [four] children: i) ADELAIDE de Louvain (-4 Nov shortly after 1158) ... m (before 5 Aug 1122) SIMON I Duke of Lorraine, son of THIERRY II Duke of Lorraine & his first wife Hedwig von Formbach'; the marriage identifies her as Duke Simon's wife per the Simon I charter naming 'uxore mea ... ducissa Adelide'
0 @S900000075@ SOUR
1 TITL WIKIPEDIA: Sikelgaita (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sikelgaita, search text read 29 Sep 2026 - exact-subject article: 'Sikelgaita (also Sichelgaita, Sigelgaita, or Gaita) (c. 1040 - 16 April 1090) was a Lombard princess, the daughter of Prince Guaimar IV of Salerno and second wife of Duke Robert Guiscard of Apulia'; infobox Born c. 1040, Died 16 April 1090, Burial Monte Cassino, Spouse Robert Guiscard, Issue incl. Maud, Roger Borsa, Guy, Robert Scalio, Sybil, Mabel, Olympias, Cecilia, Gaitelgrima, Father Guaimar IV of Salerno, Mother Gemma of Capua; married Guiscard 1058; fought in full armour at Dyrrhachium 1081; refs Balfour, Loud) + Catholic Encyclopedia (1913) / Robert Guiscard (en.wikisource.org/wiki/Catholic_Encyclopedia_(1913)/Robert_Guiscard, search text read 29 Sep 2026: 'In 1058, he had repudiated Aubree, the mother of Bohemond, to wed the Lombard Sykelgaite, sister of Gisulf, Prince of Salerno. She gave him three Sons and seven daughters, and appears to have been actively associated in all his undertakings')
0 @S900000076@ SOUR
1 TITL WIKIPEDIA: Guaimar IV of Salerno (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Guaimar_IV_of_Salerno, search text read 29 Sep 2026 - exact-subject article: 'Guaimar IV (c. 1013 - 2, 3 or 4 June 1052) was Prince of Salerno (1027-1052), Duke of Amalfi (1039-1052), Duke of Gaeta (1040-1041), and Prince of Capua (1038-1047)'; 'He was born around the year 1013, the eldest son of Guaimar III of Salerno by Gaitelgrima'; Family: 'Guaimar married Gemma, a daughter of the Capuan count Laidulf. They were married before 1032 ... Guaimar's eldest daughter was Sichelgaita, who married Robert Guiscard'; the Laidulf of Capua article (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laidulf_of_Capua, search text read 29 Sep 2026) hedges: 'Laidulf may be the father of Gemma, wife of Guaimar IV of Salerno') + fmg.ac MedLands SOUTHERN ITALY (1) ch.2 G (fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SOUTHERN ITALY, PRE-NORMAN.htm, v5.0, updated 08 Apr 2025, opened 29 Sep 2026): '1. GUAIMAR IV Prince of Salerno, [adopted] son of GUAIMAR III Prince of Salerno & his second wife Gaitelgrima of Capua ([1010/12]-murdered 3 Jun 1052)'; 'm thirdly (before May 1032) GEMMA of Capua, daughter of LAIDOLF of Capua & his first wife --- (-after Dec 1070)' - charter May 1032 names 'Gemme Principisse coniugis'; the grant in his fourteenth regnal year (1032) is at the request of 'Laidolfi comitis socero nostro' (father-in-law); Gemma's Dec 1070 Cava mill donation with the consent of her sons Gisulf, Landulf, Guido, John, and Guaimar; SICHELGAITA listed as 'daughter of GUAIMAR IV Prince of Salerno & his wife Gemma of Capua'
0 @S900000077@ SOUR
1 TITL WIKIPEDIA: Laidulf of Capua (en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laidulf_of_Capua, search text read 29 Sep 2026 - exact-subject article: 'Laidulf (Italian: Laidolfo) was a son, probably the youngest or second youngest, of Pandulf Ironhead (a 10th-century Prince of Benevento and Capua)'; 'He was the Count of Teano, and was implicated in the assassination of his brother, Landenulf, and the archbishop of Benevento in 993'; 'He succeeded his brother as Prince of Capua'; 'In 999, the Emperor Otto III came down to avenge the murder of his ally Landenulf. He removed Laidulf from power, took him as a prisoner to Germany, and placed Adhemar on the Capuan throne'; 'Laidulf may be the father of Gemma, wife of Guaimar IV of Salerno'; refs Cambridge Medieval History III) + en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Landulfids (genealogy box: 'Laidulf (died 999), Prince of Capua', son of Pandolf I Ironhead) + fmg.ac MedLands SOUTHERN ITALY (1) ch.3 A (fmg.ac/Projects/MedLands/SOUTHERN ITALY, PRE-NORMAN.htm, v5.0, updated 08 Apr 2025, opened 29 Sep 2026): '5. LAIDOLF (-after 999)' - charter dated Aug 981 names 'domini Landenolfi et Laidolfi et Gisolfi germanis tuis filii predicti domni Paldolfi principis' (Landenulf, Laidulf, Gisolf as brothers, sons of Prince Pandolf I); 'Conte di Teano'; the Cronica de Monasterio Sanctissimi Benedicti records that 'Laydolfum frater eius [=Landenulf] quo Tianus erat comitem' succeeded his brother in 992 as LAIDOLF Prince of Capua, and that he was deposed and exiled with his wife in 999; 'm MARIA, daughter of ---' (wife at the 999 exile); the Chronica Monasterii Casinensis states Laidulf agreed to the assassination of his brother when recording his exile. MedLands ch.2 G (same page, v5.0, opened this run): 'm thirdly (before May 1032) GEMMA of Capua, daughter of LAIDOLF of Capua & his first wife --- (-after Dec 1070)' - charter May 1032 names 'Gemme Principisse coniugis' as Guaimar IV's wife; a charter dated Jul 1059 quotes an earlier grant at the request of 'Laidolfi comitis socero nostro' (Laidolf the count, our father-in-law), assumed to be Guaimar IV's fourteenth regnal year (1032); Gemma's Dec 1070 Cava mill donation with the consent of her sons Gisulf, Landulf, Guido, John, and Guaimar
