2 CONT (1510-1580), English soldier and settler in Ireland; second son of John Cosby of Great
2 CONT Leake, Nottingham; settled Ireland in Henry VIII's reign; general of the Kerne 1558;
2 CONT granted the suppressed abbey of Stradbally (Queen's County) 1562; governor of Portlaoise
2 CONT and seneschal of Queen's County 1565; implicated in the Mullaghmast massacre (degree of
2 CONT responsibility unclear); killed at the battle of Glenmalure 25 August 1580. Family: married
2 CONT to Lady Mary Seymour, daughter of Lord Protector Somerset, by whom he had three sons,
2 CONT Alexander, Henry, and Arnold. Alexander succeeded to the estates, and was, with his son
2 CONT Francis, killed at the battle of Stradbally Bridge on 18 May 1596.
